        "benefits": [
          {
            "number": 1,
            "titleZh": "使用 CATCH 談論理解和潮流",
            "titleEn": "Use CATCH to talk about ideas and trends",
            "zh": "catch on 可以表示某人明白一件事，也可以表示一個新構思開始流行。",
            "en": "Catch on can show that a person understands something or that a new idea becomes popular.",
            "sourcePage": 2
          },
          {
            "number": 2,
            "titleZh": "清楚談論距離和進度",
            "titleEn": "Talk clearly about distance and progress",
            "zh": "catch up 可以表示追上前面的人，也可以表示趕上其他人的水平。",
            "en": "Catch up can show someone reaching a person ahead or reaching the same level as other people.",
            "sourcePage": 3
          },
          {
            "number": 3,
            "titleZh": "談論未完成的事情和錯過的消息",
            "titleEn": "Talk about missed work and missing information",
            "zh": "你可以 catch up on 未完成的工作，也可以 catch somebody up on 某人錯過的消息。",
            "en": "You can catch up on unfinished work or catch somebody up on news they have missed.",
            "sourcePage": 3
          },
          {
            "number": 4,
            "titleZh": "描述意外、錯誤和後來出現的後果",
            "titleEn": "Describe surprises, mistakes and later consequences",
            "zh": "catch somebody out 可以描述令人措手不及的困難或揭穿錯誤；catch up with somebody 則可以表示較早前的問題終於帶來影響。",
            "en": "Catch somebody out can describe an unexpected difficulty or reveal a mistake. Catch up with somebody can show that an earlier problem is finally having an effect.",
            "sourcePage": 3
          }
        ],
