        "benefits": [
          {
            "titleZh": "談論課堂、會議或活動後留下來",
            "titleEn": "Talk about staying after a lesson, meeting or activity",
            "zh": "wait behind 可以表示其他人離開後，某人仍然留下來。",
            "en": "Wait behind lets you explain that somebody remains after the other people have left."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "描述在不同情境中服侍別人",
            "titleEn": "Describe serving people in different situations",
            "zh": "wait on 常用於餐廳和用餐情境；wait upon 則可能出現在正式場合、古老故事和歷史劇中。",
            "en": "Wait on is useful in restaurants and meals, while wait upon may appear in formal settings, old stories and historical dramas."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "談論尚未到達的人物、消息和結果",
            "titleEn": "Talk about people, messages and results that have not arrived",
            "zh": "wait on 可以表示等候某人、送貨、回覆、價格或決定。",
            "en": "Wait on can describe waiting for a person, delivery, reply, price or decision."
          },
          {
            "titleZh": "描述安全等候，直到困難情況結束",
            "titleEn": "Describe staying safely until a difficult situation ends",
            "zh": "wait something out 可用來談論暴風雨、大雨、濃霧、塞車和其他暫時性問題。",
            "en": "Wait something out is useful when talking about storms, heavy rain, fog, traffic jams and other temporary problems."
          }
        ],
